  "body": "## What\n\nA document with no setup refuses to post a rotary program on an A-only machine. The same program posts when the document has a setup.\n\nThe post stops with this warning:\n\n```\npost: post blocked - 1 warning(s): tilted move commands B - the machine states no B rotary\n```\n\nThe machine is the built-in `Tormach 770MX + microARC 4`. Its post is `Tormach PathPilot`. The machine has an A axis about X and no B axis.\n\n## Steps\n\n1. Take `examples/catalog/multiaxis/wrapped/build.camscript` from PR for #2869.\n2. Remove the two lines `add_setup` and `set_setup_post`.\n3. Run `cargo xtask catalog --case multiaxis/wrapped`.\n\nResult: verification passes, and the post refuses with the warning above.\n\nWith the two lines, the program posts. It has A words only, and no B word.\n\n## Expected\n\nThe document post and a setup post on the same machine give the same program. A tool axis in the YZ plane needs only A on this machine. The post must not command B for it.\n\n## Notes\n\n- The refusal is safe: no wrong G-code goes out.\n- The workaround is to add a setup and set its post.\n- The program has Rotary Parallel passes that go all the way round the bar. The tool axis points straight down on the underside.\n- Found during #2869. Part of #2392.\n",
